# 🟡 PR 2 — `vanta/hono-4.12.14` Brief

## 📜 Background

`hono` is a direct dependency in two server workspaces of `normainofficial/normain`:
- `src/apps/server/api/package.json` (workspace `@normain/api`)
- `src/apps/server/tenant-api/package.json` (workspace `@normain/tenant-api`)

Both pin `hono@^4.12.4`. There are **7 open Vanta Medium alerts** against versions in this range:

| 🆔 GHSA | 📊 CVSS | 🔖 Summary | 🎯 Affected feature |
|---|---|---|---|
| 26pp-8wgv-hjvm | 5.3 | Cookie name validation in `setCookie()` | `setCookie()` w/ user-controlled names |
| 458j-xx4x-4375 | 4.3 | JSX SSR attribute injection | `hono/jsx` server-side rendering |
| r5rp-j6wh-rvv4 | 4.8 | Non-breaking space cookie prefix bypass | `getCookie()` cookie-prefix protection |
| v8w9-8mx6-g223 | 4.8 | Prototype pollution via `__proto__` | `parseBody({ dot: true })` |
| wmmm-f939-6g9c | 5.3 | Middleware bypass via repeated slashes | `serveStatic` |
| xf4j-xp2r-rqqx | n/a | Path traversal in `toSSG()` | static site generation |
| xpcf-pg52-r92g | 5.3 | IPv4-mapped IPv6 in `ipRestriction()` | IP restriction middleware |

**Reachability check (informational):** investigation showed our hono usage doesn't touch any of these features (bearer-auth, no JSX, no cookies, no serveStatic, no toSSG, no ipRestriction, plain JSON parsing). Bumping is still preferred over a reachability-based deferral because the patch is low-cost and audit optics favor active remediation.

